  "note": "Total Assets = Total Liabilities + Equity reconciles exactly. Interest income minus interest paid = net interest income exactly; PBT minus tax = net profit exactly. This source PDF is unusually long (6,177 pdftotext lines vs ~2,000 for adjacent years) — likely an appendix/annex bundled into the same filing; the Balance Sheet, P&L and classification note used here were the same clearly-labeled sections used for every other year and were fully cross-validated, so the extra bulk did not affect extraction. The bank's own 2016 Q1 report restates this quarter's EPS comparative to 0.86 (vs 0.97 contemporaneous here) — a bonus-share weighted-average-share restatement (paid-up capital rose from 5,324,591,520 at this date to 5,990,165,460 by Jun-2015, per this dataset's 2015_Q2.json, applied retroactively to this quarter's share count in the 2016 comparative). Contemporaneous value (0.97) is kept per project convention."
